<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Intuition stage (the reference abilities/cognition/intuition with the
  TypeSafe processor): the fast System 1 pick, made by the decision service
  (never by a free-text model) over the turn's choices, with the original's
  self-tuning confidence gate. The cognition (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx)
  invokes it once per turn after autonomy left the turn unhandled.

    deciding (an invoked decision service) -> done

  Processor (the original providers/typesafe Processor.process, the decision
  service's kind predicate): the turn's choices, the <param> choices (the
  body's assembled snapshot choices: its own enabled event:schema
  transitions and each ability's latest offers, tagged with the offering
  ability as target; the reference collect_offered_events), go to the
  decision service with the stimulus, which never offers the deliberate
  handoff bot.ability.reasoning.input and makes the state document {turn:
  {envelope: {name}, data}} (the original _stimulus_document) with the
  stimulus data as evidence. It asks one batch over them plus its pass criterion __unhandled__, filling
  each event's required data from the stimulus data's value, else the
  schema's enum; an event it cannot fill is not offered, so a reply that
  needs free text goes on to reasoning (user answer, 2026-10-08). When the
  pass criterion wins (declined) or nothing could be filled (no-candidates)
  the product is empty: the turn escalates with the original's reason
  empty_product and the tuner observes nothing. Otherwise the service
  returns every groundable event, each with its data and its own
  probability (decision.selected): the original's selections with their
  per-event confidences.

  Confidence (the original's ConfidenceTuner, 0-100 scale): the tuner state
  {mean, var, n}, the confidence_tuner datum, comes in as a <param> and
  goes back in <donedata>, so it lives in the cognition across turns. The
  turn's confidence is the minimum of its selections' confidences, each its
  probability normalized to a whole 0-100 number
  (<processing:selection_confidence>, the original's selection_confidence
  and normalize_confidence). <intuition:observe> observes it first (a null
  confidence is not observed), then <intuition:escalate> writes whether it
  is below the updated threshold (the original's defaults: the floor 35
  during the warmup of 8 observations, then max(floor / 2, mean - k_sigma *
  std); EMA alpha 0.08, variance floor 100), and the turn escalates when it
  is (the original's _tune_confidence, observe then should_escalate).

  Classification (the original _classify_activity, its confidence_gate off, the
  default): a confident product is handled, every selection {event, data,
  target} (escalation reason none). A low-confidence product
  (low_confidence), or one holding bot.ability.reasoning.input
  (deliberative_input), is unhandled and escalates to reasoning. The
  decision timer is deciding.after (floppy's own bound; the original's
  intuition has none).

  Dispatch (the original _dispatch_selections_activity,
  cognition.types.dispatch_selected_events): either way the stage sends
  every selection, before it answers, to its target, the session that
  offers it (the decision service names each selection's only offerer, the
  original's _single_enabler): an escalating product's are the original's
  environment actions, which it dispatches before reasoning runs; the
  ignore goes to the cognition, which only logs it, and the deliberate
  handoff is never offered. The decision service has checked each
  selection's data against its event's schema (the pinned focus device
  among them), so nothing is refused at the send; the original's
  re-ask with a rejection as feedback (routing_rejection) has nothing to
  retry.

  Output: <donedata>, received by the cognition as done.invoke.intuition:

    {turn, handled: true, selected: [{event, data, target}], reason: "none", confidence_tuner}
    {turn, handled: false, reason, confidence_tuner}  (escalate to reasoning)
    {turn, handled: false, failed: true, reason, confidence_tuner}

  A decision.failed, error.*, or no answer within decision_timeout_ms fails
  the stage (the cognition answers the turn with bot.ability.failed); the
  cognition's hop timeout bounds the whole stage too.

  Bindings: the intuition and processing namespace packages and the
  decision service package, resolved from their repository URIs; env scopes TYPESAFE_API_KEY and TYPESAFE_BASE_URL to the
  service's <invoke> (without a key it answers decision.failed
  unconfigured). An invoked service's events are not checked against
  event:schema (scxml.rs checks only events between SCXML sessions): the
  decision service validates every selection's data against the choices'
  schema for it before returning it, and its own events are shape-checked
  by cond (Object(...) reads a non-object as {}).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:intuition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/intuition"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="intuition" initial="deciding">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The turn, from the cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The bot's environment (decision D106), in the decision's
         instructions. -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <data id="confidence_tuner" expr="({mean: 70, var: 100, n: 0})"/>
    <data id="decision_timeout_ms" expr="20000"/>
    <data id="instructions" expr="'You decide what a small companion robot does with one stimulus it observed. Choose the offered event the robot should take for it. Abstain when none of them fits, so slower reasoning handles it.'"/>
    <!-- The decision in flight. -->
    <data id="confidence" expr="null"/>
    <data id="escalate" expr="false"/>
    <data id="decision_timer" expr="null"/>
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <data id="failed_code" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The selection being sent (the <foreach> item). -->
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="intuition.js"/>

  <state id="deciding">
    <onentry>
      <send idlocation="decision_timer" event="deciding.after" delayexpr="decisionTimeoutDelay()"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendidexpr="decision_timer"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke id="decision" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/decision"
            env:apikey="TYPESAFE_API_KEY" env:baseurl="TYPESAFE_BASE_URL">
      <param name="kind" expr="'predicate'"/>
      <param name="choices" expr="choices"/>
      <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
      <param name="instructions" expr="decisionInstructions()"/>
    </invoke>

    <!-- The decision service's own events. Every groundable event, each
         with its own confidence: observe their minimum, then escalate
         when it is below the updated threshold. -->
    <transition event="decision.selected" cond="hasSelections(_event)" target="done">
      <processing:selection_confidence location="confidence" selections="_event.data.selections"/>
      <intuition:observe location="confidence_tuner" confidence="confidence"/>
      <intuition:escalate location="escalate" confidence="confidence" tuner="confidence_tuner"/>
      <log label="intuition" expr="tunedLog(_event)"/>
      <if cond="escalate">
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('low_confidence')"/>
      <elseif cond="hasDeliberativeInput(_event)"/>
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('deliberative_input')"/>
      <else/>
        <assign location="result" expr="selectionResult(_event)"/>
      </if>
      <foreach array="_event.data.selections" item="s">
        <send eventexpr="s.event" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + s.target">
          <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.abstain" cond="isAbstainReason(_event)" target="done">
      <log label="intuition" expr="abstainedLog(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="abstainedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.failed" target="done">
      <assign location="failed_code" expr="failedCode(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="decisionFailedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="deciding.after" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="timedOutResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="couldNotRunResult(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The service ended without an answer: the timer decides. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke.decision"/>
  </state>

  <final id="done">
    <donedata>
      <content expr="result"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
